# Build context for the two Dockerfiles in this directory.
# This file lives at docker/.dockerignore but is consumed by
# `docker build -f docker/api/Dockerfile ...` etc. when the build
# context is the repo root.
#
# Keep build context lean and predictable: exclude venvs, notebook
# outputs, secrets, and the bulk of `models/` — re-include only the
# directory the API image needs (M3 fine-tuned weights + tokenizer).

# Python / venv / caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Tooling / VCS
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Project artifacts that don't belong in images
data/
notebooks/
tests/
docs/
infrastructure/
LICENSE
Makefile
# Note: do NOT exclude *.md — pyproject.toml points at README.md
# and hatchling errors out if it's missing from the build context.

# The trained model: exclude the bulk of `models/`, then
# re-include exactly the M3 final directory for the API image.
# The Streamlit image doesn't need any model; the api image
# copies `./models` from the build context.
models/
!models/m3-transformer/
!models/m3-transformer/final/
!models/m3-transformer/final/**

# Secrets / local config
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
